Fix semconv schema URL conflict introduced by bumping the OpenTelemetry
Go SDK to v1.44.0 for CVE-2026-41178 (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5wrp-cwcj-q835).

otel/sdk v1.44.0's process resource detector imports
go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.41.0 (see
https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/blob/v1.44.0/sdk/resource/process.go),
while descheduler's tracing package still imports semconv/v1.40.0. Mixing
schema URLs during sdkresource.New() makes tracer provider initialization
fail with "conflicting Schema URL". Align the import with the SDK's
semconv version, matching the same fix already applied for other DHI
Go application images (see image/alertmanager/patch/fix-semconv-schema-url.patch).

diff --git a/pkg/tracing/tracing.go b/pkg/tracing/tracing.go
--- a/pkg/tracing/tracing.go
+++ b/pkg/tracing/tracing.go
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@ import (
 	"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/propagation"
 	sdkresource "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/resource"
 	sdktrace "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace"
-	semconv "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.40.0"
+	semconv "go.opentelemetry.io/otel/semconv/v1.41.0"
 	"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace"
 	"go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace/noop"
 	"google.golang.org/grpc/credentials"
